  "summary": "Meyer and Ritchie's minimal imperative language over natural-number registers (increment, zero, assignment, and LOOP x DO ... END with a bound fixed on entry). LOOP programs compute exactly the primitive recursive functions; adding WHILE or GOTO gives Turing-complete languages, so the trio is a standard teaching tool for the boundary of total computation.",
